<title>FRANCE: Poliet H1 profit falls.</title>
<headline>Poliet H1 profit falls.</headline>
<dateline>PARIS 1996-09-18</dateline>
<text>
<p>Six months to end June, 1996.</p>
<p>(Figures in millions of French francs unless stated)</p>
<p>    Net attributable			     300  vs	     360</p>
<p>    Net per share		  (francs)  11.34  vs	   13.62</p>
<p>    Total Net					339  vs	     406</p>
<p>    Pre-tax, pre-exceptional		   602  vs	     691</p>
<p>    Cashflow					 715  vs	     758</p>
<p>    Turnover				    11,373  vs	  11,257</p>
<p>NOTE - The company released its results in a statement.</p>
<p>Poliet said its second-half 1996 results should show an improvement from the year-earlier period, which was hurt by strikes at the end of 1995.</p>
<p>It said only 3.8 percent of outstanding Poliet shares remain in public hands. The rest of the share capital is now owned 51.5 percent by Paribas and 44.7 percent by Cie de Saint Gobain, which also holds 97 percent Poliet's ORA's equity notes. The company has been removed from the SBF 120 and 250 indices as well as from MONEP trading. Trading in the share will be transferred to the Paris bourse cash market on September 24.</p>
<p>-- Paris Newsroom +33 1 4221 5452</p>
